{
  "application_type_full": "Tree works: Trees in conservation areas/subject to TPOs",
  "description": "T1 - Honey locust - crown reduce\r12m in height.  Reduce height by 1.5m from 12m to 10.5m.  Reduce laterals by 2m from 6m to 4m on all compass points.  An established honey locust (Gleditsia triacanthos) in the front garden of the property, standing close to the front elevation of the house and overhanging the pavement and Winterbrook Road. The tree is in reasonable physiological condition. Its crown has spread towards the building and over the street, where the extending limbs are in close proximity to the front of the house.. A moderate crown reduction will reduce leverage on the extending limbs, restore clearance from the building and keep the tree in proportion to its position.",
